# XSH cfgetispeed()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# These functions only read or write a field of a termios structure; they are tested on a zeroed
# structure and need no terminal. Rates are named by the Bxxx constants only; their encoding is
# not specified. A setter is allowed to refuse a rate (it "may fail"), so only the rates it
# accepts are compared, and at least one has to be accepted. An input speed of literal 0, and
# speeds outside the defined set, are not tested: the page leaves what is stored open.

assertion  XSH.cfgetispeed.001
anchor     functions/cfgetispeed.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/cfgetispeed.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       For each of B0 B50 B75 B110 B134 B150 B200 B300 B600 B1200 B1800 B2400
           B4800 B9600 B19200 B38400 that cfsetispeed() accepts (returns 0),
           cfgetispeed() on the structure returns exactly that value; at least
           one is accepted.
test       t/001-readback.c

assertion  XSH.cfgetispeed.002
anchor     functions/cfgetispeed.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       cfgetispeed() does not modify the structure and returns the same value
           each time it is called on it; a copy of the structure gives the same
           value.
test       t/002-pure.c
